  "summary": "Medieval wooden church with wooden posts supporting the structure.",
  "description": "Characterized by its wooden post construction with intricate dragon carvings and steeply-pitched roofs. Developed as a unique Christian architectural form that incorporated Norse artistic traditions, reflecting Norway's medieval religious and cultural identity.",
  "culturalContext": "The stave churches of Sognefjord — Urnes (UNESCO, c. 1130, oldest surviving), Borgund, Hopperstad — are Norway's medieval wooden cathedrals: stave-frame construction with carved portals in Urnes-style dragon interlace, tiered roofs with dragon-head finials, and dark tar-black timber against fjord green. Once 1,000+, twenty-eight survive; the Urnes portal's wandering animal carving is Viking-Romanesque transition's masterpiece, and the churches anchor \"fjord Norway\" cultural tourism.",
